# Project map

Stage 1 of a three-stage pipeline. Python package `stage1_scrape` under `src/`.
Layers do not mix jobs.

- `main.py` (project root) — one-command runner. Constants block, no argparse.
  Scrapes, then writes `data/exports/vendors.csv` / `.xlsx`.
  It calls `app/` and `export/`; new orchestration belongs in `app/`, not here.
- `cli.py` — argparse only (`probe`, `scrape`, `run`, `index`)
- `app/` — scrape/reindex order
- `scraping/` — HTTP to eprocure.gov.in (and captcha OCR, the only model call here)
- `parse/` — HTML → dataclasses
- `persist/` — JSON, SQLite, PDFs
- `export/` — read-only: vendor facts → CSV/Excel
- `domain/` — models, name helpers, errors

Output lives in `data/` (gitignored). Vendors, tenders and awards go to the pipeline's
shared database, defined once in `../core/` (`pipeline_core`).

Finding a vendor's email or phone is **stage 2's job** (`../02-enrich`), not this
project's. Stage 1 leaves every new vendor `enrichment_status = 'pending'` and never
writes the contact columns.

Do not put secrets in source. Load them via `stage1_scrape.settings`.
